{t:"Social Media & Self-confidence",q:"Write an essay on how social media can affect the self-confidence of teenagers.\n\nNotes:\n- It lets you share talents\n- It connects you to supportive friends\n- Too many comparisons can hurt confidence\n\n(125 to 150 words)",pts:[["Kongsi bakat: talent",["talent","share"]],["Rakan penyokong: friends / support",["friend","support"]],["Perbandingan: compar",["compar"]]],ph:["Social media has become a part of teenagers' daily lives.","On the one hand, ... On the other hand, ...","In conclusion, we should use social media wisely."],m:`Social media has become a part of teenagers' daily lives. It can build or damage our self-confidence, depending on how we use it.

Firstly, social media allows us to share our talents. For example, a student who sings well can post a video and receive kind comments. As a result, he feels proud and more confident.

Secondly, we can meet supportive friends online. They encourage us when we feel down and remind us that we are not alone.

However, some teenagers compare themselves with others too often. They see perfect photos and feel that they are not good enough. This can hurt their confidence.

In conclusion, social media is helpful if we use it wisely. We should focus on our own progress and not on other people's lives.`},
{t:"Environmental Cleanliness at School",q:"Write an essay on keeping the school environment clean.\n\nNotes:\n- Throw rubbish into the bin\n- Join the gotong-royong\n- Teachers and students share responsibility\n\n(125 to 150 words)",pts:[["Buang sampah: bin",["bin","rubbish"]],["Gotong-royong",["gotong","clean-up","cleaning"]],["Tanggungjawab bersama: responsib",["responsib"]]],ph:["A clean school gives us a healthy and comfortable place to learn.","It is our duty to ...","Everyone must play a part."],m:`A clean school gives us a healthy and comfortable place to learn. Therefore, everyone must play a part in keeping it clean.

Firstly, students should throw rubbish into the bin. If we leave rubbish on the floor, the school will look dirty and attract flies and rats. Moreover, clean toilets and a clean canteen protect us from diseases such as food poisoning and diarrhoea.

Secondly, students should join the gotong-royong programme. For example, a class can clean the drains and plant flowers together. This activity also teaches us to work as a team.

Finally, teachers and students share the responsibility. Teachers can remind us, and students must follow the rules.

In conclusion, a clean environment is possible when everyone cares. Let us keep our school clean so that we can study happily.`},
{t:"Healthy Eating Habits",q:"Write an essay on how teenagers can practise healthy eating habits.\n\nNotes:\n- Eat more fruit and vegetables\n- Drink water, not sweet drinks\n- Do not skip breakfast\n\n(125 to 150 words)",pts:[["Buah dan sayur: fruit, vegetable",["fruit","vegetable"]],["Minum air: water",["water"]],["Jangan skip sarapan: breakfast",["breakfast"]]],ph:["Healthy eating is important for growing teenagers.","One way to stay healthy is to ...","As a result, we will be more active."],m:`Healthy eating is important for growing teenagers because our body needs energy and nutrients every day. There are several ways to practise good eating habits.

Firstly, we should eat more fruit and vegetables. They are rich in vitamins and help our body fight diseases. For example, an apple or a bowl of salad is a better snack than fried chips.

Secondly, we should drink plain water instead of sweet drinks. Too much sugar can cause obesity and tooth problems. Instead, a glass of plain water keeps our body fresh and helps us concentrate better in class.

Thirdly, we must never skip breakfast. A good breakfast gives us energy to concentrate in class.

In conclusion, healthy eating habits keep us fit and active. If we start now, we will enjoy a healthier life in the future.`},
{t:"Spending & Money Management",q:"Write an essay on how students can manage their money wisely.\n\nNotes:\n- Make a budget\n- Save part of the allowance\n- Buy needs, not wants\n\n(125 to 150 words)",pts:[["Buat bajet: budget",["budget"]],["Simpan sebahagian: save",["save","saving"]],["Keperluan, bukan kehendak: need",["need"]]],ph:["Managing money wisely is a skill every student should learn.","It is wise to ...","In the long run, ..."],m:`Managing money wisely is a skill every student should learn. If we start early, we will not face money problems when we grow up.

Firstly, students should make a budget. By writing down how much we receive and spend, we know where our money goes.

Secondly, we should save part of our allowance. For example, saving just RM2 a day will become a good amount at the end of the month. This money can be used in an emergency.

Thirdly, we must buy what we need, not what we want. A new pair of shoes may look nice, but our old ones may still be good.

In conclusion, good money management brings peace of mind. In the long run, it helps us become responsible adults.`},
{t:"Malaysian Tourism & Local Culture",q:"Write an essay on why tourists should learn about local culture when they visit Malaysia.\n\nNotes:\n- Many races and festivals\n- Traditional food and clothes\n- Respect the customs\n\n(125 to 150 words)",pts:[["Pelbagai kaum dan perayaan: festival",["festival","race","culture"]],["Makanan dan pakaian: food, clothes",["food","clothes","clothing"]],["Hormati adat: respect",["respect","custom"]]],ph:["Malaysia is famous for its rich and colourful culture.","Tourists can experience ... by ...","Respecting local customs shows good manners."],m:`Malaysia is famous for its rich and colourful culture. Tourists who learn about it will enjoy their visit even more.

Firstly, Malaysia has many races and festivals. For example, tourists can join an open house during Hari Raya or watch a lion dance during Chinese New Year. These experiences show how people live together in harmony.

Secondly, tourists can try our traditional food and clothes. They can taste nasi lemak and wear a baju kurung or a sari for photos. Such activities allow them to understand our way of life and take home beautiful memories.

Finally, tourists should respect our customs, such as removing shoes before entering a house.

In conclusion, learning about local culture makes a trip meaningful. It also helps us promote Malaysia as a friendly and interesting country.`},
{t:"Kindness & Community Service",q:"Write an essay on the importance of kindness and community service.\n\nNotes:\n- Help the elderly and the poor\n- Build a caring community\n- Teaches us responsibility\n\n(125 to 150 words)",pts:[["Bantu warga emas dan miskin: elderly, poor",["elderly","poor","old"]],["Komuniti prihatin: caring",["caring","community"]],["Tanggungjawab: responsib",["responsib"]]],ph:["Kindness costs nothing, but it means a lot to others.","By helping others, we ...","In conclusion, let us spread kindness everywhere."],m:`Kindness costs nothing, but it means a lot to others. Community service is one of the best ways to show kindness.

Firstly, we can help the elderly and the poor. For example, students can visit an old folks' home and spend time with the residents. Such a visit brings joy to people who feel lonely, and even a simple conversation and a warm smile can brighten their whole day and make them feel that someone cares.

Secondly, community service helps us build a caring community. When neighbours help each other, everyone feels safe and happy.

Finally, it teaches us responsibility. We learn that we are part of society and that we must do our part.

In conclusion, kindness and community service make our world better. Let us spread kindness wherever we go.`},
{t:"Balancing Studies & Co-curricular Activities",q:"Write an essay on how students can balance studies and co-curricular activities.\n\nNotes:\n- Make a timetable\n- Do not waste time\n- Rest enough\n\n(125 to 150 words)",pts:[["Buat jadual: timetable",["timetable","schedule"]],["Jangan bazir masa: time",["time"]],["Berehat: rest",["rest","sleep"]]],ph:["Many students find it hard to balance their studies and activities.","The best way to handle this is to ...","Therefore, we can enjoy both."],m:`Many students find it hard to balance their studies and co-curricular activities. However, it is possible if we plan well.

Firstly, students should make a timetable. By setting a time for homework, revision and sports, we will not forget our duties. It also helps us to be disciplined and to complete every task on time without feeling stressed or tired.

Secondly, we must not waste time. For example, instead of scrolling through our phones, we can finish our homework before football practice. As a result, we will have more free time.

Thirdly, we need enough rest. If we are tired, we cannot concentrate in class or perform well in activities.

In conclusion, good planning helps us enjoy both studies and activities. Therefore, students should learn to manage their time wisely.`},
{t:"Digital Tools in Education",q:"Write an essay on the use of digital tools in education.\n\nNotes:\n- Learn anytime and anywhere\n- Lessons are more interesting\n- Do not misuse the internet\n\n(125 to 150 words)",pts:[["Belajar bila-bila: anytime",["anytime","anywhere","any time"]],["Pelajaran menarik: interesting",["interesting","fun"]],["Jangan salah guna: misuse",["misuse","careful","wisely"]]],ph:["Digital tools have changed the way we learn.","Not only ..., but also ...","However, we must use them responsibly."],m:`Digital tools have changed the way we learn. Tablets, laptops and learning apps are now common in many schools.

Firstly, digital tools let us learn anytime and anywhere. For example, a student can watch a science video at home if he missed a lesson.

Secondly, lessons become more interesting. Teachers can use games, pictures and videos to explain difficult topics. As a result, students pay more attention. They also remember the facts better because they can see and hear the information at the same time.

However, we must not misuse the internet. Some students play games or visit unsafe websites during lessons, which wastes their time.

In conclusion, digital tools are very helpful when we use them wisely. Both teachers and students must make sure that technology is used for learning.`},
{t:"Class Fundraising Projects",q:"Write an essay on class fundraising projects.\n\nNotes:\n- Sell food or used items\n- Raise money for a good cause\n- Teaches teamwork\n\n(125 to 150 words)",pts:[["Jual makanan atau barang terpakai: sell",["sell","sale"]],["Untuk tujuan baik: cause / charity",["cause","charity","donat"]],["Kerjasama: teamwork",["teamwork","team","cooperat"]]],ph:["Fundraising projects are popular among school students.","Our class can raise money by ...","Besides that, we learn to work together."],m:`Fundraising projects are popular among school students. They are a good way to help others and learn new skills.

Firstly, a class can raise money by selling food or used items. For example, we can bake cookies or hold a book sale during recess. Many students and teachers will gladly buy them.

Secondly, the money can be used for a good cause. We can donate it to a children's home or help a classmate who needs money for medical treatment.

Besides that, such projects teach us teamwork. Everyone has a task, from making posters to counting the money. Working together helps us to understand one another better and strengthens the bond among classmates.

In conclusion, class fundraising projects bring benefits to many people. Let us take part and make a difference.`},
{t:"Memorable Movies & Moral Values",q:"Write an essay on how movies can teach us moral values.\n\nNotes:\n- Stories about honesty and courage\n- Characters we can follow\n- Choose suitable movies\n\n(125 to 150 words)",pts:[["Cerita kejujuran dan keberanian: honesty, courage",["honest","courage","brave"]],["Watak contoh: characters",["character","hero"]],["Pilih filem sesuai: suitable",["suitable","choose"]]],ph:["Movies are not only for fun, they can also teach us lessons.","For instance, a film about ... shows that ...","Parents and teachers should guide us."],m:`Movies are not only for fun, they can also teach us important lessons. A good movie stays in our minds for a long time.

Firstly, many movies tell stories about honesty and courage. For instance, a film about a boy who returns a lost wallet shows that honesty is always the best policy.

Secondly, we can follow good characters in movies. A hero who never gives up inspires us to work hard and face our problems bravely. We learn that being honest and brave will bring a better ending in real life too.

However, we must choose suitable movies. Some movies contain violence and bad language, which can influence us badly. Parents and teachers should guide us.

In conclusion, movies can teach us moral values if we watch the right ones. Let us choose movies that make us better people.`}
